<description>
Recolor each placeholder object by the control pixel at the matching relative position inside the legend.

Input structure:
- The background is the dominant color.
- A large single-color legend body forms a rectangle containing one-pixel
  colored markers.
- Outside the legend rectangle, all foreground pixels have one placeholder
  color and form the same number of 8-connected objects as there are markers.

Rule:
- Treat the bbox of all placeholder objects as a map of their layout.
- Treat the legend bbox as the corresponding map of control-pixel positions.
- Match placeholder objects to markers by the unique minimum total distance
  between bbox-center relative positions.
- Recolor every pixel of each placeholder object with its matched marker
  color, leaving the legend and background unchanged.

Key insight:
- The gray block is a positional legend: marker locations, not marker color
  order or object shape, determine which color each outside object receives.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "8-connected placeholder-color objects s outside the grey legend rectangle",
  "dst": "colored control pixels d inside the grey legend rectangle",
  "match_cond": "s.bbox_center relative position in the placeholder-object bbox matches d.position relative to the legend bbox",
  "transform": "recolor every pixel of s with d.color",
  "symbol_instructions": "grey legend rectangle encodes the target color for each outside object by relative marker position"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 14-19 rows x 20-25 cols, background 0
  legend:
    body: solid filled rectangle of color 5 (gray), size 6-10 x 6-8
    markers: 3-5 single-pixel colored dots inside the legend rectangle
    marker_colors: all distinct, differ from bg/legend/placeholder colors
    marker_spacing: pairwise Chebyshev distance >= 2 between markers
    no bg pixels inside legend rectangle
  objects:
    count: equals number of markers (3-5)
    color: single placeholder color (not bg, not 5, not any marker color)
    connectivity: 8-connected, each 5-15 pixels, bbox 2-4 rows x 3-6 cols
    fill_ratio: 0.47-0.78 (not fully filled rectangles, have holes/notches)
    separation: pairwise Chebyshev distance >= 3 between objects
  layout:
    legend and objects-bbox do not overlap (no row/col range intersection)
    legend may touch grid edges; objects stay >= 1 cell from grid border
    min Manhattan distance from legend rect to any object pixel >= 2
  transform:
    match each object to a marker by closest relative position (object bbox-center in objects-bbox vs marker position in legend-bbox)
    recolor each object's pixels to its matched marker color; legend unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size, N markers (3-5), and N+3 distinct colors for bg(0), legend(5), placeholder, and N markers.
    2. Partition grid into two non-overlapping rectangular zones (legend zone, objects zone) with >= 2 cell gap.
    3. Place legend as a solid gray rectangle filling its zone.
    4. Choose N relative positions (well-separated) and place 1-pixel markers inside legend at those positions.
    5. Generate N random 8-connected sprites (5-15 px, bbox 2-4 x 3-6, fill 0.45-0.80) with placeholder color.
    6. Arrange sprites in the objects zone so their bbox-centers' relative positions match the markers' relative positions (this is the output-first step: assign colors to sprites = marker colors, then replace with placeholder to get input).
    7. Verify pairwise Chebyshev gaps >= 3 between objects and >= 2 to legend.
    8. Output = recolor each sprite to its matched marker color. Input = all sprites in placeholder color.
